`std::fs::write(root.join("main.go"), "package main

func One() {}
").expect("writable")` promises the compiler that this value is present, on your authority, and the reason it gives -- `writable` -- restates the problem rather than naming the invariant. The promise may well be true; what is missing is what MAKES it true. Name the invariant -- what has already validated this, and where -- so the next reader can check whether it still holds. A promise with a reason is an invariant; a promise without one is a bet, and the way you find out you lost it is a crash that explains nothing
